# http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/R67_has_part
<http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/R67_has_part> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/R67_has_part> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/R10_has_member> .
<http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/R67_has_part> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/R67i_forms_part_of> .
<http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/R67_has_part> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/F1_Work> .
<http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/R67_has_part> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/F1_Work> .
<http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/R67_has_part> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This property associates an instance of F1 Work with another instance of F1 Work that forms part of it in a complementary role to other sibling parts, conceived at some point in time to form together a logical whole, such as the parts of a trilogy. This property is transitive. \n\nIn contrast, the property R10 has member (is member of) may, for instance, also associate with the overall instance of F1 Work translations, adaptations and other derivative works that do not form a logical whole with sibling parts."@en .
<http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/R67_has_part> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "R67 has part"@en .
# 
# http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/R67i_forms_part_of
